P01 -- Canadian patent application (CIPO)

  Application no.:   3307314 (Canadian application number, regular
                     application)
  Filing date:       2026-04-06 (date of receipt, CIPO electronic submission)
  Title:             Deterministic Event-Driven Industrial Execution Engine
                     with Unified Bitfield State Architecture and
                     Type-Driven Queue Scheduling
  Applicant:         Senol Ercetin (individual application; sole inventor)
  Rights holder:     the applicant. AKYA Canada Inc. holds an EXCLUSIVE
                     LICENCE by the patent licence agreement of the filing
                     date; the application itself is not assigned. The same
                     structure applies to the copyright in the software.
  Status:            filed, pending

  Abstract (as filed):

    A deterministic industrial execution engine is disclosed comprising a
    hierarchical configuration-based data model and a unified bitfield state
    architecture. Each element includes attributes such as value and state,
    wherein the state is encoded as a unified bitfield representing runtime
    and alarm semantics. Attribute modification triggers deterministic event
    propagation across related elements. Cascaded propagation is protected
    against self-referential re-triggering and is depth-bounded to prevent
    unbounded recursion. The engine further comprises manager queues and
    worker queues for scheduling and executing events, wherein queue
    insertion behavior is determined by attribute type metadata and
    duplicate queue insertion is governed by predefined conflict resolution
    semantics. Lower-order bits of the unified bitfield encode I/O data
    quality states. The engine is deployable across heterogeneous automation
    tiers including Intelligent Electronic Devices, Remote Terminal Units,
    operator interface stations, supervisory control stations, distributed
    SCADA clusters, and cloud-based platforms.

