WHAT THIS MEANS FOR THIS REPOSITORY

  The claimed mechanisms are in the ENGINE -- AyPRO and, for the attribute
  type word, AyDATA (bin/win-x64/AyPRO.dll and AyDATA.dll,
  bin/linux-x64/libAyPRO.so and libAyDATA.so). They are not in the example
  projects.

  The example projects CONFIGURE those mechanisms, and their comments
  DESCRIBE them -- the 16-bit 'sta' field and its runtime / alarm
  configuration / command / restriction bit groups, the attribute function
  chains, the element hierarchy, the timer and queue attributes. That
  description is deliberate: an example that hides how the engine works
  teaches nothing, and this material is in the application named above,
  which will be published by CIPO in the ordinary course.

  Describing a mechanism is not a licence to implement it.

